## 3. Security Groups — Firewall Rules

### 3.1 — Recommended Security Group Configuration

| Type | Protocol | Port | Source | Purpose |
|------|----------|------|--------|---------|
| SSH | TCP | 22 | **Your IP only** | Admin access |
| HTTP | TCP | 80 | 0.0.0.0/0 | Web traffic (redirects to HTTPS) |
| HTTPS | TCP | 443 | 0.0.0.0/0 | Secure web traffic |
| Custom TCP | TCP | 3000 | 0.0.0.0/0 | *(Optional)* Direct API access |
| MySQL/Aurora | TCP | 3306 | **REMOVE THIS** | ❌ Never expose DB to internet |

> [!WARNING]
> **Port 3306 (MySQL) should NEVER be open to the internet (0.0.0.0/0).** MySQL runs inside Docker and is only accessible within the `ai_pulse_net` bridge network. Exposing it is a critical security vulnerability.

> [!WARNING]
> **SSH (port 22) should be restricted to YOUR IP address only**, not 0.0.0.0/0. Update this in AWS Console → EC2 → Security Groups → Edit Inbound Rules.

### 3.2 — How to Update Security Group Rules

```
AWS Console → EC2 → Instances → your instance
→ Security tab → Click the Security Group link
→ Edit inbound rules → Make changes → Save
```

