## 5. Docker Operations on EC2

### 5.1 — Daily Operations Cheat Sheet

```bash
# --- Navigate to project ---
cd ~/AI-PULSE-PREDICTIVE-INVENTORY-MANAGEMENT-SYSTEM-

# --- View running containers ---
docker compose ps

# --- View live logs (all services) ---
docker compose logs -f

# --- View logs for one service ---
docker compose logs -f backend
docker compose logs -f frontend
docker compose logs -f db

# --- Restart a single service (without downtime to others) ---
docker compose restart backend

# --- Full restart ---
docker compose down && docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d

# --- Pull latest images and redeploy ---
docker compose pull
docker compose up -d
```

### 5.2 — Disk Space Management (Critical!)

Docker images and logs accumulate fast on a free-tier EC2 (only 8-30 GB disk).

```bash
# Check Docker disk usage
docker system df

# Clean up unused images, containers, networks (SAFE — won't delete running containers)
docker system prune -f

# Nuclear option — cleans everything including volumes (⚠️ will delete DB data if volumes not named)
# docker system prune -a --volumes  ← DO NOT RUN unless you have a backup!

# Monitor disk weekly
df -h /
```

### 5.3 — Update the Application (Zero-Downtime Pattern)

```bash
# 1. Pull new images from Docker Hub
docker compose pull backend frontend

# 2. Recreate only updated services (db stays running)
docker compose up -d --no-deps backend frontend

# 3. Verify health
docker compose ps
curl http://localhost/api/v1/health
```

