## 7. Backups & Disaster Recovery

### 7.1 — EC2 AMI Snapshots (Full Server Backup)

```
AWS Console → EC2 → Instances → your instance
→ Actions → Image and Templates → Create Image
→ Name: "ai-pulse-backup-YYYY-MM-DD"
```

This creates a snapshot of the entire EC2 instance. You can restore from it if the instance is corrupted.

**Schedule**: Take an AMI snapshot before every major update.

### 7.2 — S3 for Static Assets & Backups

```bash
# Create S3 bucket for backups
aws s3 mb s3://ai-pulse-backups-yourname --region ap-south-1

# Enable versioning
aws s3api put-bucket-versioning \
  --bucket ai-pulse-backups-yourname \
  --versioning-configuration Status=Enabled
```

### 7.3 — Recovery Time Objective (RTO)

| Failure | Recovery Method | Time |
|---------|----------------|------|
| Container crash | `docker compose restart` | 30 seconds |
| EC2 instance terminated | Restore from AMI | 5-10 minutes |
| Database corruption | Restore from SQL backup | 10-20 minutes |
| Complete region outage | Re-deploy to another region | 30-60 minutes |

