## 8. Monitoring with CloudWatch

### 8.1 — Basic Metrics (Free Tier)

CloudWatch automatically collects these for EC2 at no cost:
- CPU Utilization
- Network In/Out
- Disk Read/Write ops

```
AWS Console → CloudWatch → Metrics → EC2 → Per-Instance Metrics
```

### 8.2 — CloudWatch Alarms (Set These Up!)

**High CPU Alarm:**
```
CloudWatch → Alarms → Create Alarm
→ Metric: EC2 → CPUUtilization
→ Threshold: Greater than 80% for 2 consecutive 5-min periods
→ Action: Send email to your address via SNS
```

**Instance Status Check Alarm:**
```
→ Metric: StatusCheckFailed
→ Threshold: >= 1
→ Action: Email alert
```

### 8.3 — Application-Level Monitoring (Advanced)

Add structured logging to Node.js backend and ship logs to CloudWatch:

```bash
# Install CloudWatch agent on EC2
sudo apt install amazon-cloudwatch-agent

# Configure it to watch Docker logs
sudo nano /opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/config.json
```

```json
{
  "logs": {
    "logs_collected": {
      "files": {
        "collect_list": [
          {
            "file_path": "/var/lib/docker/containers/**/*-json.log",
            "log_group_name": "/ai-pulse/docker",
            "log_stream_name": "{hostname}",
            "timestamp_format": "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

