## 9. Cost Optimization

### 9.1 — Monthly Cost Breakdown (Typical)

| Service | Free Tier | After Free Tier |
|---------|-----------|-----------------|
| EC2 t2.micro | Free (12 months) | ~$8-10/month |
| Elastic IP | Free (when associated) | Free |
| S3 (backups) | 5GB free | ~$0.023/GB |
| CloudWatch (basic) | Free | Free |
| Data Transfer | 15GB/month free | $0.09/GB |
| **Total** | **~$0** | **~$10-15/month** |

### 9.2 — Cost Saving Tips

```bash
# 1. STOP the instance when not demoing (saves compute cost)
#    AWS Console → EC2 → Stop Instance
#    ⚠️ Data in volumes is preserved, Elastic IP remains

# 2. Use Spot Instances for non-critical workloads (up to 90% cheaper)
#    Not recommended for your primary demo server

# 3. Set up AWS Budgets alert
#    AWS Console → Billing → Budgets → Create Budget
#    → Alert when cost exceeds $10/month
```

### 9.3 — AWS Free Tier Alert

```
AWS Console → Billing → Billing Preferences
→ Enable "Free Tier Usage Alerts"
→ Enter your email
```

> [!CAUTION]
> The EC2 t2.micro free tier expires **12 months** after your AWS account creation. After that, you'll be charged. Set a Budget alert to avoid surprise bills.

