## 10. CI/CD — GitHub Actions + AWS

### 10.1 — Current Workflow Summary

Your `.github/workflows/` likely has a pipeline that:
1. Builds Docker images
2. Pushes to Docker Hub
3. SSHs into EC2 and runs `docker compose pull && docker compose up -d`

### 10.2 — Improved CI/CD with AWS SSM (No SSH Keys in GitHub!)

Instead of storing your EC2 SSH private key in GitHub Secrets (risky), use **AWS Systems Manager (SSM)**:

```yaml
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml
- name: Deploy via SSM (no SSH keys needed)
  uses: aws-actions/aws-ssm-send-command@v1
  with:
    instance-ids: ${{ secrets.EC2_INSTANCE_ID }}
    document-name: AWS-RunShellScript
    parameters: |
      commands:
        - cd /home/ubuntu/AI-PULSE-PREDICTIVE-INVENTORY-MANAGEMENT-SYSTEM-
        - docker compose pull
        - docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d --no-deps backend frontend
        - docker compose ps
```

**GitHub Secrets to set:**
| Secret Name | Value |
|-------------|-------|
| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` | IAM deploy-bot access key |
| `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | IAM deploy-bot secret key |
| `EC2_INSTANCE_ID` | `i-0abc123...` |
| `DOCKERHUB_USERNAME` | Your Docker Hub username |
| `DOCKERHUB_TOKEN` | Docker Hub access token |

### 10.3 — Deployment Strategy

```
Push to main branch
      │
      ▼
GitHub Actions runs tests
      │
      ▼
Build Docker images (multi-stage)
      │
      ▼
Push to Docker Hub (backend:latest, frontend:latest)
      │
      ▼
SSM Command → EC2 pulls new images
      │
      ▼
docker compose up -d (rolling update)
      │
      ▼
Health check: curl /health
```

